**Subjec:t** Discussion on Public Services and Policy Implementation --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **CC:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 5, 2023 **Subject:** Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi John, I hope this message finds you well. Following our recent meeting on February 28, 2023, regarding the implementation of new regulations affecting public services in our city, I wanted to share some thoughts and next steps. As you're aware, the new public service regulations introduced by the State Policy Agency (SPA) aim to improve accessibility and efficiency in public service delivery. These regulations, wihch take effect on July 1, 2023, require the City Government to align our current systems with the updated compliance standards. **Key Points from the Meeting:** 1. **Regulatory Framework**: The SPA has outlined specific compliance measures that need to be addressed, including customer service training for all public-facing employees and the integration of a new digital service platform. 2. **Budget Implications**: We discussed the necessity of reallocating approximately $500,000 from the city budget to fund these initiatives, especially for the training programs and technology upgrades. 3. **Timeline**: We need to establish a timeline for implementing these regulations, ensuring that all departments are onboard by the end of June. Could you provide an update on the state’s readiness to support us in the training aspect? Lisa has been working on identifying suitable training vendors, but we'd appreciate any insights from your end. Looking forward to your response. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **CC:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 6, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi Sarah, Thank you for your email and the detailed summary of our meeting. I agree that aligning our efforts is crucial for a successful implementation of the new regulations. **Regarding your inquiries:** 1. **Training Support**: The SPA is prepared to assist with training resources. We recommend collaborating with the Public Service Training Institute (PSTI), which specializes in customer service and compliance training. They have a proven track record and can tailor their programs to meet our specific needs. 2. **Budget Recommendations**: The state can offer a grant of up to $200,000 to support training initiatives. However, we must submit the grant application by April 15, 2023, and outline how it will be utilized effectively. 3. **Project Timeline**: I suggest we set up a follow-up meeting to finalize the timeline and ensure all departments are informed. I am available next week on Tuesday or Thursday afternoon. Let me know what works for you. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **Date:** March 7, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi Sarah and John, I appreciate the updates. I’ve already started reaching out to PSTI for their course outlines and availability. I’ll ensure they understand the urgency of our timeline. Regarding the grant application, I suggest we prepare a detailed budget plan that outlines how we will allocate the funds within the $500,000 budget. This would strengthen our application and demonstrate responsible financial planning. I can draft a preliminary budget proposal by March 20, 2023, if that works for everyone. Additionally, I think it would be beneficial to include Mark in our next meeting to discsus the technology upgrades that will be necessary for the new digital service platform. Looking forward to hearing from you. Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** March 8, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi all, Thanks for including me in this conversation. I agree that engaging PSTI for training is a good move. As for the technology upgrades, I’d like to add that we should consider a phased approach to minimize disruption to service delivery. **Proposed Tech Upgrade Phases:** 1. **Phase 1 (April - June 2023)**: Upgrade existing software systems to ensure they are compatible with the new digital service platform. 2. **Phase 2 (July - September 2023)**: Implement the new digital platform across all departments. 3. **Phase 3 (October 2023 and onwards)**: Full staff training and customer outreach to educate the public on the new system. I’ll prepare a technical requirement document outlining the specific upgrades needed and their associated costs by the end of next week. Let’s coordinate our schedules for a follow-up meeting. I am available on Thursday afternoons as well. Best regards, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 10, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi all, Thank you for the insights. I think we are making good progress. Here’s what I propose: 1. **Set a Meeting**: Let’s aim for Tuesday, March 14, 2023, at 2 PM for our follow-up meeting. We can discuss the training details with PSTI, finalize the budget proposal, and review the technical requirements from Mark. 2. **Grant Application**: Lisa, can you lead the preparation of the grant application? I’ll assist you with the necessary documentation. 3. **Communication Plan**: We should also discuss how we will communicate these changes to the public to ensure a smooth transition. Please confirm your availability for Tuesday. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 11, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi Sarah, Tuesday at 2 PM works for me. I’ll prepare some additional materials regarding the training grant and gather any other resources that may assist us. I also recommend we consider a public forum post-implementation to gather feedback from residents on the new services. This could enhance community engagement and trust in our processes. Looking forward to our meeting! Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 12, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi everyone, I’m in for Tuesday at 2 PM. I’ll have the preliminary budget proposal ready by then, and I can also start drafting an outline for our communication plan regarding the upcoming changes. I think John’s idea of a public forum is excellent. Perhaps we can schedule it for late July, after the initial rollout of the new platform, to allow residents to provide feedback and address any concerns. Looking forward to our discussion! Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** March 13, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Follow-up on Public Services Policy Implementation Hi team, I’m confirming my availability for the meeting on Tuesday at 2 PM. I’ll have the technical requirements document finalized by then. Regarding the public forum, I suggest we partner with local community centers to promote the event and ensure a diverse group of residents can attend. See you all tomorrow! Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 14, 2023 **Subject:** Meeting Reminder: Public Services Policy Implementation Hi all, Just a reminder about our meeting today at 2 PM. I look forward to reviewing the budget, the technical requirements, and our training plans wiht PSTI. Let’s ensure we are on track for the July implementation deadline. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 14, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Meeting Reminder: Public Services Policy Implementation Hi Sarah, I appreciate the reminder. I’ll be ready with the training resources and grant application details for our discussion. Looking forward to it. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 14, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Meeting Reminder: Public Services Policy Implementation Hi team, I’m all set for our meeting today. I’ve drafted the preliminary budget and an outline for the communication plan. See you soon! Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** March 14, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Meeting Reminder: Public Services Policy Implementation Hi everyone, I’m ready for the meeting. The technical requirements document is complete, and I’m excited to share it with you all. See you shortly. Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson 