hompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** March 21, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Budget Proposal Draft Review Hi team, I’m available for the review session on March 22, 2023, at 10 AM. I’ll also present the updated technical requirements based on the latest feedback. See you then! Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 22, 2023 **Subject:** Review Session Summary Hi team, Thank you for a constructive review session this morning. Here are the action items moving forward: 1. **Final Budget Proposal**: Lisa will incorporate feedback and finalize the budget proposal for submission by the end of the week. 2. **Training with PSTI**: John will finalize arrangements with PSTI and confirm the training schedule. 3. **Technical Requirements**: Mark will circulate the updated technical requirements document by March 24, 2023. Let’s keep up the momentum as we approach the implementation deadline. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 23, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Review Session Summary Hi Sarah, I’m in the process of finalizing the training schedule with PSTI. I expect to have their confirmation by March 27, 2023. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 23, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Review Session Summary Hi everyone, I’m finalizing the budget proposal and will ensure it is submitted by March 31, 2023. I’ll keep you all in the loop as I progress. Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** March 24, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Review Session Summary Hi team, The updated technical requirements document is attached for your review. Please provide any feedback by March 28, 2023, so we can finalize it. Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 25, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Review Session Summary Hi team, I’ve reviewed the technical requirements document and appreciate Mark’s updates. I recommend we have a brief meeting on March 30, 2023, to finalize everything before the budget submission deadline. Please confirm your availability. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 26, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Review Session Summary Hi Sarah, I’m available for a meetign on March 30, 2023. I’ll also have the training confirmation from PSTI by then. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 26, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Review Session Summary Hi everyone, I’m also available for the meeting on Mrach 30, 2023. I’ll ensure the budget proposal is ready for review. Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** March 26, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Review Session Summary Hi team, I’m available for the meeting on March 30, 2023. I’ll bring the finalized technical requirements document for our discussion. Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 30, 2023 **Subject:** Final Meeting Summary Before Submission Hi team, Thank you for a productive meeting today. Here are the final action items: 1. **Budget Proposal**: Lisa will submit the budget proposal by March 31, 2023. 2. **Training Confirmation**: John will confirm the training schedule with PSTI and share it with the team. 3. **Technical Requirements**: Mark will distribute the finalized technical requirements document. Let’s ensure we meet our deadlines and maintain clear communication with the SPA as we move forward with the implementation. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 31, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Final Meeting Summary Before Submission Hi Sarah, I received confirmation from PSTI on the training scheudle. We will begin training sessions on May 15, 2023, with a focus on customer service and compliance. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** March 31, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Final Meeting Summary Before Submission Hi team, I have submitted the budget proposal as planned. We should expect feedback from the SPA by mid-April. Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** April 1, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Final Meeting Summary Before Submission Hi all, I will circulate the finalized technical requirements document by April 3, 2023. I also think it would be beneficial to draft a user guide for the new digital service platform to assist staff during the transition. Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 2, 2023 **Subject:** Next Steps for Implementation Hi team, As we move closer to the implementation date of July 1, 2023, let's ensure we have the following in place: 1. **Training Sessions**: John, please keep us updated on PSTI's training program. 2. **Public Communication**: Let’s start drafting our communication plan for the public forum and the rollout of the new services. 3. **Monitoring and Evaluation**: We should discuss how we’ll monitor the implementation and gather feedback from both staff and residents. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 3, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Next Steps for Implementation Hi Sarah, I will ensure the training sessions with PSTI are well-advertised and that all relevant personnel are informed. I’ll also prepare a follow-up communication for the team regarding the training topics and schedules. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarha Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 3, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Next Steps for Implementation Hi everyone, I’ll begin drafting the communication plan and will include strategies for engaging with underserved communities. I’ll circulate a draft by April 15, 2023, for review. Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** April 3, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Next Steps for Implementation Hi team, I’ll draft the user guide for the new digital service platform and share it with everyone by April 20, 2023. This guide will be essential for staff as they transition to the new system. Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 5, 2023 **Subject:** Communication Plan Draft Hi team, As we approach the implementation phase, I wanted to touch base regarding the communication plan. Here are a few points I believe we should include: 1. **Announcement of Changes**: A press release to inform the public about the new regulations and services. 2. **Public Forum**: Details and dates for the public forum to solicit feedback. 3. **Engagement Strategies**: Targeted outreach to community organizations, especially those serving underserved populations. Please let me know if you have any additional thoughts or if you’d like to discuss this further. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 6, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Communication Plan Draft Hi Sarah, I think your points are excellent. I would also suggest we include a FAQ section on our website to address common questions about the new services and the transition process. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 6, 2032 **Subject:** Re: Communication Plan Draft Hi everyone, I can include a section on addressing community concerns and providing resources for additional support as part of the communication plan. This will ensure that residents know where to turn if they need help or have questions. Best, Lisa --- **From:** Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **Date:** April 6, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Communication Plan Draft Hi team, I’ll ensure the user guide includes links to the FAQ section and other resources mentioned in our communication plan. This will help staff and residents navigate the new system more smoothly. Best, Mark --- **From:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org> **To:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 10, 2023 **Subject:** Update on Implementation Steps Hi team, As we move closer to the implementation date, let's ensure we are on track with the following: 1. *F*inalize Training Schedule**: John, please confirm the finalized training schedule with PSTI and share it with the team. 2. **Communication Plan**: Lisa, please circulate the draft communication plan by April 15, 2023, for feedback. 3. **User Guide**: Mark, I look forward to seeing the user guide and ensuring it aligns with our communication strategies. Best, Sarah --- **From:** John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 11, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Update on Implementation Steps Hi Sarah, I have confirmed the training schedule with PSTI. Training will begin on May 15, 2023, and will run for four weeks. I will share the detailed schedule with everyone shortly. Best, John --- **From:** Lisa Raymond <lisa.raymond@citygov.org> **To:** Sarah Thompson <sarah.thompson@citygov.org>, John Martinez <john.martinez@statepolicy.org>, Mark Chen <mark.chen@citygov.org> **Date:** April 12, 2023 **Subject:** Re: Update on Impleme